{"assets":["/statement-assets/2b67e7ee87a2c072e85f6d93c2979c7ab8846e3ee6982bd1394748a45fe69f69.png"],"contentKind":"statement","contestId":"1380","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"attrs":{"level":1,"role":"title"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"F. Strange Addition"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"time_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"time limit per test"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"5 seconds"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"memory_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"memory limit per test"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"256 megabytes"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"body"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Let $$$a$$$ and $$$b$$$ be some non-negative integers. Let's define "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"strange addition"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" of $$$a$$$ and $$$b$$$ as following:"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"attrs":{"ordered":true},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" write down the numbers one under another and align them by their least significant digit; "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" add them up digit by digit and concatenate the respective sums together. "}],"kind":"list_item"}],"kind":"list"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Assume that both numbers have an infinite number of leading zeros."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"For example, let's take a look at a "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"strange addition"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" of numbers $$$3248$$$ and $$$908$$$:"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/statement-assets/2b67e7ee87a2c072e85f6d93c2979c7ab8846e3ee6982bd1394748a45fe69f69.png"},"kind":"image"}],"kind":"container"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"You are given a string $$$c$$$, consisting of $$$n$$$ digits from $$$0$$$ to $$$9$$$. You are also given $$$m$$$ updates of form: "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"attrs":{"ordered":false},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" $$$x~d$$$ — replace the digit at the $$$x$$$-th position of $$$c$$$ with a digit $$$d$$$. "}],"kind":"list_item"}],"kind":"list"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Note that string $$$c$$$ might have leading zeros at any point of time."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"After each update print the number of pairs $$$(a, b)$$$ such that both $$$a$$$ and $$$b$$$ are non-negative integers and the result of a "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"strange addition"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" of $$$a$$$ and $$$b$$$ is equal to $$$c$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Note that the numbers of pairs can be quite large, so print them modulo $$$998244353$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"input_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The first line contains two integers $$$n$$$ and $$$m$$$ ($$$1 \\le n, m \\le 5 \\cdot 10^5$$$) — the length of the number $$$c$$$ and the number of updates."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The second line contains a string $$$c$$$, consisting of exactly $$$n$$$ digits from $$$0$$$ to $$$9$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Each of the next $$$m$$$ lines contains two integers $$$x$$$ and $$$d$$$ ($$$1 \\le x \\le n$$$, $$$0 \\le d \\le 9$$$) — the descriptions of updates."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"output_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Print $$$m$$$ integers — the $$$i$$$-th value should be equal to the number of pairs $$$(a, b)$$$ such that both $$$a$$$ and $$$b$$$ are non-negative integers and the result of a "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"strange addition"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" of $$$a$$$ and $$$b$$$ is equal to $$$c$$$ after $$$i$$$ updates are applied."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Note that the numbers of pairs can be quite large, so print them modulo $$$998244353$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"samples"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Example"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n2 3\n14\n2 4\n2 1\n1 0\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n15\n12\n2\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"note"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Note"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"After the first update $$$c$$$ is equal to $$$14$$$. The pairs that sum up to $$$14$$$ are: $$$(0, 14)$$$, $$$(1, 13)$$$, $$$(2, 12)$$$, $$$(3, 11)$$$, $$$(4, 10)$$$, $$$(5, 9)$$$, $$$(6, 8)$$$, $$$(7, 7)$$$, $$$(8, 6)$$$, $$$(9, 5)$$$, $$$(10, 4)$$$, $$$(11, 3)$$$, $$$(12, 2)$$$, $$$(13, 1)$$$, $$$(14, 0)$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"After the second update $$$c$$$ is equal to $$$11$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"After the third update $$$c$$$ is equal to $$$01$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"document"},"index":"F","problemCode":"1380F","schema":2,"sourceKind":"html","sourceUrl":"https://codeforces.com/contest/1380/problem/F"}